2026-06-06T19:49:22Z	Matt Reider	accepted	termkrush/Pitch-preserving-time-stretch.md	Offline pitch-preserving time-stretch engine: audio::time_stretch(samples, channels, ratio) — overlap-add (Hann, 50% synthesis hop, analysis hop = hop/ratio), per-channel, normalized. Pitch preserved by construction (windows never resampled); only spacing/duration changes. Verified: ratio 1.0 is a bit-identical round-trip; output length scales with ratio (±1 window); pitch (zero-cross rate) preserved within 5% across a 1.5x stretch; finite. SCOPE: delivered the reusable offline engine (what clip auto-BPM #47 consumes — clips are pre-stretched then played straight, so no realtime-callback cost / no xrun risk). The story's *deck* real-time tempo-ratio + on-device xrun check is deferred: varispeed (,/.) already gives deck tempo (pitch-changing); a pitch-preserving deck mode via pre-stretch is a follow-up. OLA is clean for beat-match ratios (±8%); WSOLA/phase-vocoder refinement later if transient smearing matters. all suites green; fmt/clippy clean.
